From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 21:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] sdcard: report what the PIO data loop costs

ISSUE-0013 proposes porting dma.resource and a DMA SD path, and its own first
acceptance criterion is the one nobody has met: what fraction of a boot is the
card. Without that number the best case is unknown, and the issue says so --
"if the answer is 5%, the best possible outcome here is 2.5 s".

This measures it, and measures the right thing. The brackets go around the PIO
word loop and nothing else -- not the command setup, not the inter-block
polling -- because that loop is exactly what a DMA path would replace. What
comes out is therefore the *ceiling* on what ISSUE-0013 could ever be worth,
which is the number that decides whether to spend the work.

That loop is where PIO is paid for: a 512-byte block is 128 MMIO reads, each
one executed as JITted m68k code.

Reporting is per megabyte rather than per transfer, so the instrument does not
change what it measures; serial output at block rate would dominate the
result. SYSTIMER_CLO is 1 MHz, so the accumulator is microseconds and wraps
after about 71 minutes, far beyond any boot being measured.

Enabled on __EMU68__ rather than on request. On this port the card is the boot
medium and PIO is a deliberate choice recorded in soc/sdcard/mmakefile.src, so
what that choice costs belongs in every boot log next to the rest of the
bring-up trace.

Upstream carries no accounting here, and would not want this as written -- the
enable is target-specific.

See AI_context/consolidated/history/ISSUE-0013.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 rom/devs/sdcard/sdcard_bus.c | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 52 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rom/devs/sdcard/sdcard_bus.c b/rom/devs/sdcard/sdcard_bus.c
--- a/rom/devs/sdcard/sdcard_bus.c
+++ b/rom/devs/sdcard/sdcard_bus.c
@@ -40,6 +40,39 @@
 
 /* Generic "Bus Unit" Functions */
 
+/*
+ * On this port the card is the boot medium and PIO is a deliberate choice, so
+ * what it costs is worth knowing on every boot rather than on request.
+ */
+#if defined(__EMU68__)
+#define SDCARD_PIO_ACCOUNTING
+#endif
+
+#if defined(SDCARD_PIO_ACCOUNTING)
+/*
+ * How much of a boot is spent moving card bytes a longword at a time?
+ *
+ * This brackets the PIO word loop below and nothing else -- not the command
+ * setup, not the inter-block polling -- because that loop is precisely what a
+ * DMA path would replace. The number it produces is therefore the *ceiling* on
+ * what ISSUE-0013 could ever be worth, which is the question that gates it.
+ *
+ * A 512-byte block is 128 MMIO reads, each executed as JITted m68k code, so
+ * this is the one place where the choice of PIO is paid for per longword.
+ *
+ * SYSTIMER_CLO is 1 MHz, so the accumulator is in microseconds and wraps after
+ * about 71 minutes -- far longer than any boot being measured. Reporting is
+ * per megabyte rather than per transfer so the instrument does not perturb
+ * what it measures; serial output at block rate would dominate the result.
+ */
+#define SDCARD_PIO_REPORT_BYTES (1UL << 20)
+
+static ULONG sdcard_pio_us = 0;
+static ULONG sdcard_pio_bytes = 0;
+static ULONG sdcard_pio_blocks = 0;
+static ULONG sdcard_pio_next = SDCARD_PIO_REPORT_BYTES;
+#endif
+
 /* How long a single block may keep the PIO transfer waiting */
 #define SDHCI_DATA_TIMEOUT_US   1000000
 
@@ -1056,6 +1089,9 @@
     ULONG               waitStart = 0;
     BOOL                waiting = FALSE;
     ULONG               retVal = 0;
+#if defined(SDCARD_PIO_ACCOUNTING)
+    ULONG               pioStart;
+#endif
 
     DFUNCS(bug("[SDBus%02u] %s()\n", bus->sdcb_BusNum, __PRETTY_FUNCTION__));
 
@@ -1126,6 +1162,9 @@
                 volatile ULONG *dataPtr = (volatile ULONG *)sdData;
 
                 DTRANS(bug("[SDBus%02u] %s: Attempting to %s %dbytes\n", bus->sdcb_BusNum, __PRETTY_FUNCTION__, ((sdDataMode == MMC_DATA_READ) ? "read" : "write"), tranlen));
+#if defined(SDCARD_PIO_ACCOUNTING)
+                pioStart = sdcard_CurrentTime();
+#endif
                 if (sdDataMode == MMC_DATA_READ)
                 {
                     for (currword = 0; currword < tranwords; currword++)
@@ -1140,6 +1179,19 @@
                         bus->sdcb_IOWriteLong(SDHCI_BUFFER, dataPtr[currword], bus);
                     }
                 }
+#if defined(SDCARD_PIO_ACCOUNTING)
+                sdcard_pio_us += sdcard_CurrentTime() - pioStart;
+                sdcard_pio_bytes += tranlen;
+                sdcard_pio_blocks++;
+                if (sdcard_pio_bytes >= sdcard_pio_next)
+                {
+                    bug("[SDBus%02u] PIO: %lu KiB in %lu ms, %lu blocks\n",
+                        bus->sdcb_BusNum, (unsigned long)(sdcard_pio_bytes >> 10),
+                        (unsigned long)(sdcard_pio_us / 1000),
+                        (unsigned long)sdcard_pio_blocks);
+                    sdcard_pio_next += SDCARD_PIO_REPORT_BYTES;
+                }
+#endif
                 sdData += tranlen;
                 sdDataLen -= tranlen;
                 waiting = FALSE;
